WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.180
The Supreme Court

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.580
is about to decide

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.620
do you have to pay union dues

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:07.120
if your workplace is unionized?

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.480
When I worked at

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.960
CBS and ABC,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.940
I had to.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.260
I was told,

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.120
this is a union shop.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.860
You must pay up.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.280
But now the court may say for government workers,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.060
that's unconstitutional.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.260
So unions are nervous.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.960
If we lose this case,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.020
the entire public sector will be right to work.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.740
Right to work would mean

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.880
unions could no longer

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.280
force workers to join

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.620
and pay dues.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.500
The union's values are all money.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.940
Teacher Rebecca Friedreichs

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.360
filed a lawsuit that

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.800
went to the Supreme Court

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.040
because she says,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:41.540
unions

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.520
are bullies.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.900
If someone

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.400
takes something from me.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.286
You understand why she says that

00:00:47.286 --> 00:00:48.160
when you

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.180
listen to some union leaders speak.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.100
And I'm going to punch you in the face

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.860
and push you in the dirt.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.040
That guy is boss

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.100
of the biggest teachers union.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.780
And you sick people.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.620
Rebecca got mad at her union

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.220
during the last recession

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.440
when she tried to save some teachers jobs

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.140
by getting all the teachers

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.600
to take a slight pay cut.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.020
They were willing to take a cut?

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.980
Absolutely.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.799
We're willing to have that discussion

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:14.459
and all of America was taking a pay cut pretty much.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.900
Why should we be any different?

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.960
But the union wouldn't even allow her to survey

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.580
the other teachers.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.360
They said absolutely not.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.720
Would not let me send out that survey.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.160
Then, angering her further:

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.500
They told me,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.660
"Rebecca, don't worry about those teachers

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.277
who are going to lose their jobs.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.260
The union's going to take care of them.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.920
We're going to give them

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.560
a seminar

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.860
on how to get unemployment benefits."

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.480
So Rebecca decided

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.900
she no longer wanted to pay union dues.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.603
She sued the California Teachers Association

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.954
and after three years,

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.200
the Supreme Court heard her case.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.860
This is so exciting.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.560
Our voices were heard today.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.500
Union voices were heard too.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.100
They protested on the steps outside the court.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.580
We fight for equality.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.860
They were worried

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.860
because Supreme Court watchers said

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:02.900
Rebecca was likely to win.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.560
The case that has the potential

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.420
to decimate

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.320
the way that public sector unions function.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.300
But then,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.131
Supreme Court Justice Antonin Scalia has died.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.400
That was the most devastating day.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.797
Without Scalia's vote, the court deadlocked.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.500
That meant unions could continue

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.476
forcing teachers to pay dues.

00:02:19.476 --> 00:02:21.859
It is a huge win for public sector unions.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:22.960
But now a new case

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.640
filed by this government worker

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.760
Mark Janus

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.440
is about to be heard by the court.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.413
With Neil Gorsuch,

00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:29.579
the ninth justice,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.160
unions are so worried

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.260
they even agreed to speak to me.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.140
Our members want their union.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.400
They want their union

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.800
to have power.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:39.560
Steve Kreisberg represents the union

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.624
that's being sued

00:02:40.624 --> 00:02:42.040
by Mark Janus.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:42.833
It's his right

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:43.920
to dissent

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.300
and not be a member of our union.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.460
He only has to pay the fees

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.620
that are used to represent him.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.680
What's the point in that

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.980
if you have to pay?

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:51.993
That's the main reason

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.440
he doesn't want to join.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.560
He doesn't want to be forced to pay for something

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.160
he doesn't agree with.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.072
Well, I'm not sure

00:02:58.072 --> 00:02:59.440
if he doesn't agree with it

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.020
or if he just simply doesn't want to pay

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:01.900
because he'd like to get those

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:02.860
services for free.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.960
The union could say,

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.080
"We're bargaining

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.720
for all you teachers.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.840
If you don't

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.619
join the union,

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.000
you're a free rider."

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.460
I never asked for their representation.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.720
All right, but you're getting it

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.220
and presumably benefitting.

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.720
If I saw their

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.720
representation as a benefit,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:19.900
then I could agree with that.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.679
But I don't see it as a benefit.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:22.322
Their benefits

00:03:22.322 --> 00:03:22.873
aren't worth

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:24.280
the moral costs.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:24.880
To me,

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:25.560
that sounds like the words

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.800
of a right-wing activist,

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.280
not the words of a teacher.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.400
She was a teacher

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.240
who got together with other teachers

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.100
and said

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.380
let's take a pay cut

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.720
so nobody has to get fired,

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:35.900
and the union said "No,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.100
you may not even put that to a vote."

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.900
They elected somebody else.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.980
So she has no more right

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.120
to call a vote

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.513
than Hillary Clinton has the right

00:03:44.513 --> 00:03:45.520
to conduct foreign policy

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.940
for the United States of America.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.820
Thomas Jefferson believed that

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.560
to compel a man to contribute

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.433
to propagation of opinions

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.200
to which he disbelieves

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.040
is sinful

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.200
and tyrannical.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.640
Thomas Jefferson

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.200
had no sense

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.940
of 21st century labor relations.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:01.860
It is mine!

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.600
No, he probably didn't.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.600
You do not take what is mine!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.013
Now the Supreme Court

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:07.820
will decide.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.611
Oral arguments

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.420
are scheduled for Monday.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.080
The court will announce its decision

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.800
sometime this summer.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:14.740
I hope they'll see it

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.560
the way Jefferson did.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.960
Forcing someone

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.820
to pay for something they don't want

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.160
is tyranny.

